# Devgentic — .gitignore
#
# Created 2026-08-05. The repo had none, which is why `build/` (SPM checkouts + DerivedData) and
# per-user Xcode state were being picked up by `git add`.
#
# ⚠️ Adding a path here does NOT untrack what is already committed. Anything listed under
# "already tracked" below still needs `git rm --cached` to stop being versioned.

# ── Build output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This project builds with `-derivedDataPath build/DerivedData`, so everything under build/ is
# regenerable: DerivedData, SPM checkouts/artifacts, XCBuildData, test results.
build/
DerivedData/
*.xcarchive
*.ipa
*.dSYM.zip
*.dSYM

# ── Xcode per-user state ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ⚠️ xcuserdata is per-developer (window layout, breakpoints, scheme ordering) and churns on every
# session. SHARED schemes live in xcshareddata/ and MUST stay tracked — devgentic.xcscheme and
# devgenticTests.xcscheme carry the test-isolation environment variables (G55), so ignoring
# xcshareddata would silently un-isolate everyone's test runs.
xcuserdata/
*.xcuserstate
*.xcuserdatad
*.moved-aside
*.perspectivev3

# ── Swift Package Manager ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.build/
.swiftpm/
Packages/
# Package.resolved IS tracked on purpose — it pins dependency versions for reproducible builds.

# ── Claude Code / agent working state ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Worktrees are checkouts of this same repo; committing the gitlink makes the parent repo depend on
# a directory that only exists on one machine (and is what left an orphaned session record here).
#
# ⚠️ The `**/` prefix is LOAD-BEARING, not decoration. These rules were once written as
# `.claude/worktrees/` and `.claude/settings.local.json`; a pattern containing a slash is
# anchored to this file's directory, so both matched ONLY the repo root. Claude Code creates
# `.claude/` relative to the session's working directory, so a session started deeper in the
# tree wrote `Devgentic/Interfaces/Main/Views/Tooling/Local/.claude/settings.local.json` —
# which no rule matched, and it was committed in `a3b831d` carrying absolute home paths and a
# personal document's filename. Match at ANY depth, or this recurs the next time someone runs
# an agent from a subdirectory.
**/.claude/worktrees/
**/.claude/settings.local.json

# ── macOS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
Icon?
._*

# ── Local build settings ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Per-machine signing identity for Debug builds (see Config/Debug.xcconfig).
Config/Local.xcconfig

# ── Local scratch ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ⚠️ NOT `logs/` or `*.log`: the repo-root `logs/` directory holds captured investigation
# transcripts that are deliberately tracked and cited from `observability_baseline.md`.
#
# ⚠️ These four are the EXCEPTION to that, named individually rather than by widening the rule.
# They are real captured sessions that name personal employment documents by filename, so they
# must not be published — but `logs/` stays tracked, so nothing else here would catch them and a
# later `git add -A` would pull them straight back in. Excluded 2026-09-05; they remain on disk.
logs/MistralXMLParser_not_found_log.txt
logs/ask_tool_permission_access_log.txt
logs/report_1_log.txt
logs/response_synthesizer_edge1_log.txt

*.tmp

# ── Harnesses' own build output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ToolHarness/ and MCPHarness/ are SwiftPM packages at the repo root; their sources are tracked,
# their build products are not.
ToolHarness/.build/
MCPHarness/.build/

# ── Public-release working notes ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ⚠️ These are PRIVATE remediation notes and must never be published. They name the
# commits that still hold personal data (a government ID, home paths) and the private
# Bitbucket workspace — publishing them would index the PII instead of removing it,
# which is the opposite of their purpose. Untracked 2026-09-10; they stay on disk.
Public_Release_Checklist.md
Public_Release_Roadmap.md
SCRUB_MANIFEST.md
#
# ⚠️ The internal readiness / design / audit registers are the same class: they enumerate
# open defects by name and cite commit hashes. D10 (2026-09-10) decided they do not ship.
# Matched by SHAPE, not one-by-one — `git add -A` swept ChatOps_Production_Readiness.md
# into a commit precisely because the earlier rules named individual files.
*_Production_Readiness*.md
*_Readiness*.md
*_Audit*.md
*_Design*.md
*_Prompt*.md
*_Plan*.md

# ⚠️ AND THE WHOLE FOLDER. `Planout/` is where development documents live from 2026-09-13 on —
# readiness registers, audit findings, design notes, release checklists, agent plan artifacts.
# Ignoring it by DIRECTORY rather than by filename shape is the point: the shape rules above are
# `*_Plan*.md`, so `p3_batch_plan.json` (lowercase, .json) walked straight past them into a
# `git add -A` — the fourth time an internal register has been swept into a commit that way.
# These documents enumerate open defects by name and cite commit hashes; D10 (2026-09-10) decided
# they do not ship. `architecture_readme.md` moved in here too and was untracked in the same
# change — it is the living invariant register, and its authoritative copy has always been the
# one on disk.
Planout/

# ── SQLite sidecars beside the SwiftData store fixtures ──────────────────────────
# Opening a .store in WAL mode creates -wal and -shm beside it, so any test run that
# reads the fixtures leaves six untracked files. They are per-run state, never fixture
# content, and a later `git add -A` would sweep them in — which is exactly how a stray
# binary reached HEAD in 2faad1c. The .store files themselves stay tracked.
*.store-wal
*.store-shm

# ── Stray compiled scratch binaries at the repo root ─────────────────────────────
# `swiftc foo.swift` with no -o writes an executable named `main` next to the source.
# One reached HEAD in 2faad1c via `git add -A` and shipped in the tip commit.
# ⚠️ The leading slash is deliberate: it anchors this to the repo ROOT only, so it can
# never shadow a legitimate file or directory called `main` deeper in the tree.
/main

# 2026-09-18 — three more sweeps caught before the first public push. Shape-matched, per the rule above.
# `.swift-cache/` is a clang/Swift module cache (`<hash>/*.pcm`, 62 MB); it was STAGED by a `git add -A`.
.swift-cache/
# ObjectBox's generator writes `model-<target>.json.bak` next to the model file it rewrites. The model
# file itself MUST stay tracked (entity UIDs); the backup never should be.
*.bak
# One-off analysis pages belong in Planout/ (ignored above), not the repo root.
/workflow_comparison.html
# 2026-09-18 — Code mode's per-project memory file. Pointing Code mode at THIS folder wrote
# `Devgentic/.devgentic/context.md`, which the synchronized group then copied into every built
# app as `Contents/Resources/context.md`. Any project's `.devgentic/` is agent state, never source.
**/.devgentic/

# Local Xcode derived data redirected into the repo (hidden dot-folder variant of DerivedData/).
.derivedData/
